# Session and video UI legibility

Sessions are recorded in **presenter mode** and published on **YouTube (1080p)**. Every user-visible label, body line, code bubble, and control must read **at a glance on a TV-sized stream** — not just on a laptop at arm's length.

**Default assumption: you are designing a slide, not a dense app UI.**

If in doubt between two sizes — always pick the **larger** one. Fewer words at larger size beats more words at small size.

**Simple English is mandatory** — `.cursor/rules/session-simple-english.mdc`. Short plain words on every label; no jargon unless it is the concept being taught.

## Typography — hard minimums (never go below)

| Role | Tailwind floor | Preferred on full-slide panels |
|---|---|---|
| In-component headings (`h2`/`h3`) | `text-xl md:text-2xl` | `text-2xl md:text-3xl` |
| Body / explanations / step detail | `text-lg md:text-xl` | `text-xl md:text-2xl` |
| Section labels ("USER INPUT", "TOKENS", etc.) | `text-base md:text-lg` | `text-lg md:text-xl` — always `font-bold` |
| API / JSON / monospace payloads | `text-base md:text-lg` | `text-lg md:text-xl` in hero code bubbles |
| Buttons / toggles / step controls | `text-base md:text-lg` | `py-3 px-5` minimum tap target |
| Secondary / hint copy | `text-base` | Never use `text-sm` even for hints |

## Absolutely banned — zero exceptions

- `text-xs` anywhere in teaching UI
- `text-sm` as primary or secondary teaching copy
- Arbitrary small sizes: `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-[12px]`, `text-[13px]`
- Faint labels on dark shells: `text-gray-500` or dimmer for anything the presenter reads aloud
- Wrapping long explanations into tiny condensed pills just to fit more on one slide — **split into a new slide instead**

## Contrast requirements

- **Dark shells:** body text `text-gray-100`–`text-gray-200`; secondary text minimum `text-gray-300`
- **Light shells:** body text `text-gray-800`–`text-gray-900`; secondary minimum `text-gray-600`
- Never rely on color alone to distinguish active vs inactive states — use size or weight too

## Blocks and spacing

- **Outer panels:** `p-8 md:p-10` for full-slide interactives; `space-y-6`–`space-y-10` between major blocks
- **Inner cards:** `p-5 md:p-6` minimum
- **Chips / pills:** `py-3 px-4` minimum; hero rows `text-lg md:text-2xl` with `ring-1` or border for separation on video
- Do not shrink padding to fit more content — **remove content instead**

## Presenter viewport fit — one screen, no scroll (mandatory)

Interactives are shown under a large `##` title in **presenter mode** (`?view=present`). The animation must **fit on one slide** below the HUD and title — not a tall scrollable page.

**Design for the slide, not the article view.**

**Long slides are a recording defect.** If the presenter must scroll to read the active step on a 1080p stream, the slide is too tall — fix it before shipping.

### What “fits” means

- The **active step** of an animation should be readable **without vertical scrolling** on a 1080p presenter viewport. **Zero scroll is the bar**, not a nice-to-have.
- **Short and compact beats complete and tall.** Prefer the smallest layout that still teaches the idea — one row, one diagram band, one caption line.
- **Clear, big text** (see typography table above) **and** **short copy** — large type does not excuse long paragraphs or extra rows.
- Prefer **one teaching frame per step**: e.g. stage header → **Before / After** → optional one-line footer. Good reference: `CommonCrawlPreparationFlow` after slim-down.
- Use **internal step-through** (Prev / Play / Next, tabs, phases) to reveal more — **never stack duplicate panels** on the same step (e.g. Input/Action/Output + “At a glance” + full walkthrough = too tall for PPT).
- **Prefer tabs over long vertical stacks.** If a step has multiple examples, sequences, sources, or variants (e.g. Sequence 1 + Sequence 2, Corpus A + Corpus B), show **one at a time via tabs** — not stacked cards below each other. Good references: `Gpt3DataSourcesExplorer`, `PreTrainingLoopExplorer` (batch sequence tabs), `RNNWorkingExample`.

### Slide height budget — cut rows before you cut type

When the active step feels tall:

1. **Remove a row** — weight grids, token grids, and card lists default to **one row** (3 items). Never use two rows on a busy step.
2. **Remove a section** — drop redundant headers, duplicate footers, or a second teaching panel on the same step.
3. **Add a tab or internal step** — move the extra content behind navigation instead of stacking it vertically.
4. **Never** shrink type or padding to cram more in — that violates legibility and still scrolls on video.

### Copy length limits (teaching UI)

- **Before / After labels:** 2–4 words (`Before`, `After`, or `Before — plain text`).
- **Body lines:** 1–2 short sentences per panel, or a **small concrete example** (URL, one HTML line, token grid preview) — not walls of text.
- **Monospace / JSON / WARC snippets:** show the **minimum** that teaches the idea; truncate with `…` when the full payload is not needed on video.
- **Token grids / tables / weight samples:** **one row only** (3–4 items) on slide-scale panels; “… + N more” in the caption for the rest. Two-row grids are an anti-pattern when the step already has a header, diagram, or tabs.
- If the idea needs more detail → **next step** or **next slide**, not smaller text or more stacked sections.

### Anti-patterns (reject on sight)

- **Multiple examples stacked vertically** on one step (Sequence 1 block, then Sequence 2 block, then Sequence 3…) — use **tabs** or **Prev/Next** instead; only the active item should be visible.
- Three or more **independent vertical sections** teaching the same step (summary cards + hero diagram + full walkthrough).
- Tiny SVG or `text-sm` labels in a large empty box — use **HTML + large type**, not illegible diagram placeholders.
- **Scrolling the presenter slide** to read the animation — split the component, remove a row/section, or add steps. A slide that scrolls is not shippable.
- **Two-row grids or card lists** on steps that already have tabs, a hero diagram, or a loss/header block — use one row + “… + N more” instead.

### When building or editing animations

1. **Large type first** — never ship small text to “fit more in.”
2. **Then cut height** — remove duplicate sections until the active step fits one screen.
3. **Spot-check** in `?view=present` before finishing; if you must scroll, simplify.

## SVG and diagrams

- All SVG label text: **16px+ in user units** (equivalent to `text-base` or larger)
- Avoid 9–10px axis labels; only tick marks may be that small, and only when the axis label above them is large
- Node labels, edge labels, step names inside SVGs: 16px+ minimum; 18–20px preferred

## Enforcement on new and edited components

- Any **new** session-facing component must meet this rule from the very first commit
- When editing an existing component, **upgrade all typography in that component** to meet these minimums — do not leave old small text alongside new large text
- **Accuracy is independent of legibility** — never ship wrong teaching content to fit the slide; see `.cursor/rules/session-educational-accuracy.mdc`
- Non-user-facing code (`lib/`, types, tests) is exempt, but do not re-export tiny UI from shared session barrels
